# {{ .AppName }}

## Prerequisites
* JDK 25
* Docker and Docker Compose
{{- if .SpringAISupport }}

This application uses [Spring AI](https://docs.spring.io/spring-ai/reference/) with the following chat model providers:
{{- if .OllamaSupport }}
* **Ollama** (`ollama`) - runs locally. `compose.yml` includes an `ollama` service, and the `local` profile pulls the configured model (`OLLAMA_CHAT_MODEL`, default `llama3.2`) on first use.
{{- end }}
{{- if .OpenAISupport }}
* **OpenAI** (`openai`) - set the `OPENAI_API_KEY` environment variable.
{{- end }}
{{- if .AnthropicSupport }}
* **Anthropic** (`anthropic`) - set the `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` environment variable.
{{- end }}

The active chat model is selected by the `spring.ai.model.chat` property (default: `{{ .DefaultAIChatModel }}`).
To switch providers, set the `SPRING_AI_MODEL_CHAT` environment variable to one of: {{ range $i, $m := .SpringAIModels }}{{ if $i }}, {{ end }}`{{ $m }}`{{ end }}.

Use `AiChatService` (or inject `ChatClient.Builder`) to talk to the model.
{{- end }}

{{ if .TaskfileSupport -}}
## Using Taskfile
This project uses [Taskfile](https://taskfile.dev/) to run common tasks defined in `Taskfile.yml`.

Install the JDK and {{ .BuildTool }} versions configured in `.sdkmanrc` using [SDKMAN](https://sdkman.io/):

```shell
$ curl -s "https://get.sdkman.io" | bash
$ source "$HOME/.sdkman/bin/sdkman-init.sh"
$ sdk env install
```

Install Task by following the [installation guide](https://taskfile.dev/docs/installation) (ex: `brew install go-task`).

```shell
# List available tasks
$ task --list

# Format code and run tests
$ task format
$ task test

# Run verification checks
$ task verify

# Build docker image
$ task build_image

# Run application in docker container
$ task start
$ task stop
$ task restart
```
{{- end }}
{{- if .MiseSupport -}}
## Using mise
This project uses [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev/) to install the required SDKs and run common tasks defined in `mise.toml`.

Install mise by following the [installation guide](https://mise.jdx.dev/getting-started.html) (ex: `brew install mise`).

```shell
# Trust the project's mise.toml (one-time)
$ mise trust

# Install the SDKs (Java 25 Temurin, {{ .BuildTool }})
$ mise install

# List available tasks
$ mise tasks

# Format code and run tests
$ mise run format
$ mise run test

# Run verification checks
$ mise run verify

# Build docker image
$ mise run build_image

# Run application in docker container
$ mise run start
$ mise run stop
$ mise run restart
```
{{- end }}

{{- if .AxelixSupport }}
## Axelix

This project includes the [Axelix](https://axelix.io/) Spring Boot 4 starter and build plugin.
The plugin bundles project metadata into the application during the build.
{{- if eq .BuildTool "Gradle" }}
Axelix {{ .AxelixVersion }} requires Gradle's configuration cache to be disabled.
If you enabled it globally, pass `--no-configuration-cache` to Gradle commands.
{{- end }}

Connect the service to Axelix Master using the
[starter configuration guide](https://axelix.io/docs/start/configuring-spring-boot-starter).
Configure the same JWT signing key and algorithm in Master and this service before deploying.
The dedicated Spring Security filter chain delegates `/actuator/axelix-*/**` authentication to Axelix,
which validates Master's JWT. Other endpoints use the application's security configuration.
{{- end }}
